---
// The practical questions someone asks before installing. The numbers come from the palette and the port
// registry, so the answers cannot drift from what ships.
import DisclosureIcon from "./DisclosureIcon.astro";
import { PORT_REQUEST, REPO, TEXT_ROLES, flavors, ports, shipped, short } from "../lib/data.mjs";
import { h2, section } from "../lib/ui.mjs";

const list = (items: string[]) => new Intl.ListFormat("en", { type: "conjunction" }).format(items);
// Browser ports can share a subset; every port declares its own supported flavors.
const partial = ports.filter((p) => shipped(p).length < flavors.length);
const full = ports.length - partial.length;
const subset = partial.length ? list(shipped(partial[0]).map(short)) : "";
const browserException = partial.length > 0 && partial.every((p) => ["firefox", "chrome"].includes(p.id) && shipped(p).map((f) => f.id).join() === shipped(partial[0]).map((f) => f.id).join());

const a = "text-fg underline decoration-accent/50 transition-colors hover:text-accent";
---

<section class={section} id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="grid gap-y-10 gap-x-[clamp(40px,6vw,96px)] lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,1.3fr)]">
    <h2 class:list={[h2, "self-start"]} id="faq-title" data-reveal>A few things<br /><span class="text-accent">before you switch.</span></h2>
    <div class="border-t border-line">
      <details class="faq-item border-b border-line" name="faq">
        <summary><span>Which flavor should I start with?</span><DisclosureIcon /></summary>
        <p class="max-w-[40em] pb-7 text-fg-alt">Night, unless you have a reason not to. It is the default: dark slate and the full palette. Frost takes a third of the chroma out for long sessions, Paper is for daylight, and Signal keeps one accent and lets slate do the rest. <a class={a} href="#flavors">Try them above</a> and this page repaints.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item border-b border-line" name="faq">
        <summary><span>Does every port include all four flavors?</span><DisclosureIcon /></summary>
        <p class="max-w-[40em] pb-7 text-fg-alt">
          {ports.length === 0
            ? "No ports are published yet. "
            : partial.length === 0
            ? ports.length === 1 ? "Yes. The published port includes all four. " : `All ${ports.length} do. `
            : browserException
              ? `${full} of ${ports.length} do. ${partial.length === 2 ? "Both" : "The"} browser themes ship ${subset} only: a browser theme colors little more than backgrounds, borders and one accent, so Frost and Signal would look like Night there. `
              : `${full} of ${ports.length} do. Other ports ship a smaller selection. `}
          Each port's page lists the flavors it ships.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item border-b border-line" name="faq">
        <summary><span>Do I need to clone the repository?</span><DisclosureIcon /></summary>
        <p class="max-w-[40em] pb-7 text-fg-alt">No. Each app installs the way it normally installs things: from its marketplace or built-in theme list where one exists, otherwise with one command you copy from the <a class={a} href="/ports/">port's page</a>.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item border-b border-line" name="faq">
        <summary><span>What do the contrast checks cover?</span><DisclosureIcon /></summary>
        <p class="max-w-[40em] pb-7 text-fg-alt">Every color used for text: the foreground, the syntax roles, diagnostics, links and the active line number, {TEXT_ROLES.length} roles in all. The build fails if any of them drops below 4.5:1 (WCAG AA) against its flavor's background. Colors that are not text, such as borders, selection and inactive line numbers, are not held to it.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item border-b border-line" name="faq">
        <summary><span>My app isn't listed. Now what?</span><DisclosureIcon /></summary>
        <p class="max-w-[40em] pb-7 text-fg-alt"><a class={a} href={PORT_REQUEST}>Request a port</a> and name the app. Meanwhile, anything with color settings can follow the theme: map the <a class={a} href={`${REPO}#using-the-palette-in-something-else`}>semantic roles</a> onto its slots or read the values from <a class={a} href={`${REPO}/blob/main/palette.json`}>palette.json</a>. If you build one, <a class={a} href={`${REPO}#contributing-a-port`}>contributing a port</a> explains how to add it.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq-item summary {
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 24px;
    min-height: 64px; padding-block: 24px; cursor: pointer; list-style: none;
    font-size: 1.125rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }
  .faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .faq-item summary:hover { color: var(--lc-accent); }
</style>
